1. airplay2-sender-cpp
   Copyright 2026 Andreas Wendorf (Akustikrausch)
   https://github.com/akustikrausch/airplay2-sender-cpp
   Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

   The AirPlay 2 sender used by this app is a vendored, patched copy of this
   project, located in `airplay2-sender-cpp/`. It carries its own LICENSE,
   NOTICE and licenses/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, which remain authoritative for
   that component. The patches applied by CastBridge are:

     a. AirPlay 2 transient-pairing event-channel key derivation. Upstream
        derives the Events keys only in the pair-verify path; on the HAP
        transient path used by HomePods the event channel is therefore never
        keyed and the receiver tears the session down after ~30 s. CastBridge
        derives the Events keys in the transient path as well.

     b. Ring-buffer latency management in the streaming example (connect-phase
        drain, then a bounded drift splice above 1.6 s of queued audio).

   CastBridge's modifications are licensed under the Apache License 2.0, the
   same terms as the upstream project.

2. Mbed TLS 3.6
   Copyright (c) The Mbed TLS Contributors
   https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls
   Licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (used here under the Apache-2.0
   option; Mbed TLS is also offered under GPL-2.0-or-later).

   Included as a git submodule at `third_party/mbedtls`, pinned to commit
   2ca6c285a0dd3f33982dd57299012dacab1ff206 (v3.6.0), together with its own
   `framework` submodule. Provides the SRP-6a bignum mod-exp, SHA-512 /
   HMAC-SHA512, HKDF-SHA512, ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD, X25519 ECDH and CTR-DRBG
   used by the AirPlay pairing code. Upstream airplay2-sender-cpp fetches this
   dependency over the network at build time; CastBridge vendors it so the
   build is self-contained and needs no network access.

3. ed25519 (orlp/ed25519)
   Copyright (c) 2015 Orson Peters
   https://github.com/orlp/ed25519
   Licensed under the zlib license.

   Vendored by airplay2-sender-cpp under
   `airplay2-sender-cpp/third_party/ed25519` (pinned commit b1f19fab). Provides
   the Ed25519 sign/verify and X25519 primitives that Mbed TLS 3.6 does not
   offer, used in the AirPlay 2 pair-verify exchange.

4. pyatv and pair_ap (credited; no source bundled)
